-- Silver Support Scheme Act 2015 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation in force from 1 December 2025 -- LAYER 1, THE NOUNS.
--
-- Entities, facts and choices only: DECLARE and nothing else (no rule, no #EVAL).
-- Every other sssa-*.l4 module imports this one.
--
-- The membership test for this file: could a witness of ordinary competence
-- testify to the fact, or does answering it need the Act?  Only the first kind
-- belongs here.  "Is a public officer" is a fact about a person's post that a
-- witness can give; "is an administrator" is a rule and lives in
-- sssa-part1-preliminary.l4.
--
-- Terms the Act borrows from other instruments that are not among the sources
-- (public officer, public Act, public function, written law, citizen of
-- Singapore, the Immigration Act 1959, the Central Provident Fund Act 1953) are
-- asked as facts, as the brief rules.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 2: when a person is born (s 6(2))
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- What can be ascertained about the date of birth.  s 6(2)(c): the day of the
-- month "cannot be ascertained"; s 6(2)(d): the month "cannot be ascertained".
-- The text is silent about a year that cannot be ascertained, so the year is
-- also a MAYBE: NOTHING means "not ascertained".
DECLARE `Birth facts` HAS
    `year of birth`  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `month of birth` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `day of birth`   IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- s 7(2): a class of eligible individuals and the amount prescribed for it.
-- The class and the amount are both set by regulations that are not among the
-- sources, so a caller states them.
DECLARE `Class amount` HAS
    `class of eligible individual` IS A STRING
    `amount prescribed`            IS A NUMBER

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 1: facts about the bodies and persons the definitions in s 2 pick out
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 2 "administrator".
DECLARE `Body asked about as an administrator` HAS
    `is the Board`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a public officer`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a public authority`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `has been appointed by the Minister under section 5(4) to assist the Board` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 2 "Commissioner" and s 4(1), (2): how the person came to hold the post.
DECLARE `Appointment under section 4` IS ONE OF
    `appointed under section 4(1) as the Commissioner for Silver Support`
    `appointed under section 4(2)(a) as a Deputy Commissioner for Silver Support`
    `appointed under section 4(2)(b) as an Assistant Commissioner for Silver Support`
    `not appointed under section 4`

-- s 2 "investigator".
DECLARE `Person asked about as an investigator` HAS
    `is an officer or employee of the Board authorised under section 5(7) to conduct an investigation under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has been appointed under section 5(8) to assist the Board in conducting an investigation under this Act`         IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 2 "means information".
DECLARE `Information asked about as means information` HAS
    `relates to the income or assets of an individual`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `relates to the income or assets of a group of individuals who comprise a household`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in the possession of a Government department or public authority`                       IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 2 "public authority".
DECLARE `Body asked about as a public authority` HAS
    `is a body established or constituted by or under a public Act`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `is to perform or discharge a public function`                    IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 2 "public scheme", paragraphs (a) and (b).
DECLARE `Scheme asked about as a public scheme` HAS
    `is or will be established by or under written law`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `is or will be administered by a public authority`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `is or will be administered by the Government in any other manner`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `is to provide financial relief, assistance or support to citizens of Singapore`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `is to provide financial relief, assistance or support to permanent residents of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is to provide financial relief, assistance or support to a part of those citizens or permanent residents` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The capacities in which a person can act under the Act.  ss 8(7), 9(1), 19.
-- `someone else` means none of the capacities the Act names.
DECLARE Capacity IS ONE OF
    `the Commissioner for Silver Support`
    `a Deputy Commissioner for Silver Support`
    `an Assistant Commissioner for Silver Support`
    `the Board`
    `a member, officer or employee of the Board`
    `an administrator who is a public officer`
    `an administrator that is a public authority other than the Board`
    `a public officer or employee of a public authority acting under the Commissioner's direction`
    `a public officer acting under the direction of an administrator who is a public officer`
    `a member, officer or employee of an administrator that is a public authority other than the Board`
    `an investigator`
    `someone else`

-- s 8(7) "information recipient" and "officer": the recipient asked about.
DECLARE `Information recipient asked about` IS ONE OF
    `a Commissioner who is a public officer`
    `a Commissioner who is an employee of a public authority`
    `the Board as recipient`
    `an administrator who is a public officer as recipient`
    `an administrator that is a public authority other than the Board as recipient`

-- s 8(7) "officer": how the person stands to the recipient.
DECLARE `Relation to the information recipient` IS ONE OF
    `the recipient itself`
    `a public officer acting under the recipient's direction`
    `an employee of the same public authority acting under the Commissioner's direction`
    `a member, officer or employee of the Board`
    `a member, officer or employee of the administrator`
    `no relation the Act names`

-- ss 8 and 9: the two kinds of information.
DECLARE `Kind of information` IS ONE OF
    `means information`
    `confidential information other than means information`

-- s 8(3): what the authorised person does with the means information of an
-- individual who has opted out.
DECLARE `Act on means information` IS ONE OF
    `accessing means information about the individual obtained under section 8(1)`
    `using or disclosing under section 9 means information about the individual that was previously accessed`
    `any other act`

-- s 8(4)(b) and (c): the conduct of an officer of an information recipient.
-- Paragraph (b) is about an authorised person and means information obtained under
-- section 8(1); paragraph (c) is about any officer and confidential information
-- (other than means information) obtained under section 8(2).
DECLARE `Conduct of an officer of an information recipient` HAS
    `is an officer of an information recipient`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an authorised person`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `acts in good faith`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `acts with reasonable care`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `accesses the information`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `discloses the information to another officer of the same information recipient`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `that other officer is an authorised person`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information is means information obtained under section 8(1)`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the information is confidential information other than means information obtained under section 8(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct is in the performance of duties connected with the administration or enforcement of this Act or the administration of the Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 9(2): a use or disclosure of the information obtained under section 8.
DECLARE `Use or disclosure asked about under section 9(2)` HAS
    `is of means information obtained under section 8(1) or of confidential information other than means information obtained under section 8(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is without the consent of the individual to whom the information relates`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `has the purpose of communicating or managing the information as part of the administration or enforcement of this Act`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `has the purpose of communicating or managing the information as part of the administration of the Scheme`                       IS A BOOLEAN

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 3: recovery (s 10)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 10(3): where an administrator may recover from.
DECLARE `Source of recovery` IS ONE OF
    `a cash grant or other benefit the recipient is eligible to receive under the Scheme`
    `another sum payable to the recipient by the administrator`
    `another source`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 4: power to obtain information (s 14)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 14(1): who is requiring.
DECLARE `Person requiring` IS ONE OF
    `the Commissioner`
    `an investigator as requirer`
    `someone else as requirer`

-- s 14(1): the purpose the requirer is acting for.
DECLARE `Purpose of the requirement` IS ONE OF
    `reviewing the administration of the Scheme or the disbursement or conferment of a benefit`
    `conducting an investigation under this Act`
    `another purpose`

-- s 14(1)(a), (b), (c): what is required.
DECLARE `Thing required` IS ONE OF
    `to attend, answer a question or give a signed statement`
    `to provide information within the person's knowledge`
    `to produce a document or record for inspection`
    `to allow the original of a document or record to be retained, or copies made`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 4: composition (s 17) and regulations (s 20)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 17(1): who collects the sum.
DECLARE `Who compounds` IS ONE OF
    `the Board`
    `an officer or employee of the Board who is authorised by the Board in writing`
    `an officer or employee of the Board who is not authorised by the Board in writing`
    `someone else as compounder`

-- s 20(2)(a) to (i): what regulations may be made about.
DECLARE `Matter for regulations` IS ONE OF
    `the benefits under the Scheme, including different amounts of benefits for different classes of eligible individuals`
    `the method and manner of disbursing or conferring each benefit under the Scheme by an administrator`
    `the terms and conditions for each benefit under the Scheme`
    `the assessment by an administrator of an individual's eligibility for any benefit under the Scheme, and of the amount of the benefit payable to the individual`
    `the review by the Commissioner of any assessment, and the time within which the application for the review must be made`
    `how any administrator appointed under section 5(4) may assist the Board in administering the Scheme, including different roles for different administrators or classes of administrators`
    `how any investigator appointed under section 5(8) may assist the Board in conducting any investigation under this Act`
    `the fees to be paid for any thing or matter done or to be done under this Act in respect of which it appears to the Minister to be expedient to charge fees`
    `anything that is required or permitted to be prescribed under this Act`
    `another matter`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 4: bodies corporate and others (s 16)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `Kind of entity` IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary body corporate`
    `a limited liability partnership as defined in section 2(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005`
    `a partnership`
    `an unincorporated association other than a partnership`
    `some other entity`

-- s 16(5) "officer", paragraph (a): in relation to a body corporate.
DECLARE `Position in a body corporate` IS ONE OF
    `a director`
    `a partner`
    `a member of the board of management`
    `a chief executive`
    `a manager`
    `a secretary`
    `another similar officer of the body corporate`
    `a person purporting to act in one of those capacities`
    `no such position`

-- s 16(5) "officer", paragraph (b): in relation to an unincorporated association
-- other than a partnership.
DECLARE `Position in an unincorporated association` IS ONE OF
    `the president`
    `the secretary of the association`
    `a member of the committee`
    `a person holding a position analogous to president, secretary or member of a committee`
    `a person purporting to act in one of those capacities in the association`
    `no such position in the association`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Penalties (ss 8(6), 9(7), 11(1), 14(4), 15, 17, 20(3))
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The most a court may impose.  Each Act provision says "a fine not exceeding $x
-- or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding n months or ... both", so the
-- penalty is a pair of ceilings and never an amount to pay.
DECLARE Penalty HAS
    `greatest fine in dollars`                  IS A NUMBER
    `greatest imprisonment in months`           IS A NUMBER

-- The offences in the Act, for s 17(1) (compounding) and the seat layer.
DECLARE `Offence under the Act` IS ONE OF
    `the offence in section 8(6)`
    `the offence in section 9(7)`
    `the offence in section 11(1)`
    `the offence in section 14(4)`
    `the offence in section 15`

-- s 19(4): the liabilities the section says it leaves in place.
DECLARE `Kind of liability` IS ONE OF
    `liability under section 20 of the Financial Procedure Act 1966`
    `liability under section 8(6)`
    `liability under section 9(7)`
    `any other liability`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The regulative rules (parties and acts)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `A party under the Act` IS ONE OF
    `the Government department or public authority`
    `the authorised person`
    `the Commissioner, the Board or the administrator`
    `the person required`
    `the collector of the compounded sum`

DECLARE `An act under the Act` IS ONE OF
    `provide the information to the authorised person`
    `provide the information to the information recipient`
    `access the means information`
    `use or disclose the means information`
    `provide a report about the individual`
    `provide the information or produce the document or record`
    `pay the sum into the Consolidated Fund`
